see a `1.0.0` release of git-bug, we should have this feature implemented\n\nas far as implementation details go, i'm very much in favor of leaning on the design of namespaces as much as possible.\n\n\u003e If that would also help against merge conflicts, that would be great. I have no idea though since I don’t know how git bug is implemented.\n\ngit-bug's [data model](https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/blob/4d053ace27ca110b646a6b8d5801afdda669efe4/doc/design/data-model.md) is designed in such a way that merge conflicts are not possible.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1747855159,"nonce":"N/nV39tEEjA+3zEDlBEVljYATDo=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh86syvC_","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/75#issuecomment-2898981055"},"message":"@LemmingAvalanche sorry, i thought i had sent this earlier, but apparently not.\n\n\u003e I also don’t want to use SHA-1 for bug ids. git bug probably probably doesn’t support incrementing ids so I’ll probably just do it manually. Then with my namespace the issues could be identified with \u003cnamespace\u003e-\u003cinteger\u003e.\n\nunfortunately, incrementing identifiers are not possible in a distributed system -- the closest we _could_ get is to support a mode in which git-bug connected to a centrally managed server to get an ID, but this is not on the roadmap.","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1747855184,"nonce":"lXAQoo68Oqzt2Dh+/GH4VrVXyPg=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOCGKeh86syvC_zmfqkq4"},"target":"d0391439ed00829038b3a6295503a66e73dccedb11dd793e19cb935995c7696f","message":"@LemmingAvalanche sorry, i thought i had sent this earlier, but apparently not.\n\n\u003e I also don’t want to use SHA-1 for bug ids. git bug probably probably doesn’t support incrementing ids so I’ll probably just do it manually. Then with my namespace the issues could be identified with \u003cnamespace\u003e-\u003cinteger\u003e.\n\nunfortunately, incrementing identifiers are not possible in a distributed system -- the closest we _could_ get while maintaining the bulk of the distributed behavior is to support a mode in which git-bug connected to a centrally managed server to get an ID, but this is not on the roadmap.","files":null}]}